{"id":"2a2b22aeccc3a68f","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-norm.md","title":"Norm","display":"df-norm — Norm","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-norm","aliases":["58-df-norm","Norm","Normed Space"],"display":"df-norm — Norm","depends_on":["[[58-df-vector-space]]","[[58-df-metric-space]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-norm"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-norm</span><span>Norm</span><span>Normed Space</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-norm — Norm"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Norm}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\">\\(\\mathrm{Norm}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\">\\(\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> (vector space over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\">\\(\\mathbb{R}\\)</span> or <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{C}\">\\(\\mathbb{C}\\)</span>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{F}\\in\\{\\mathbb{R},\\mathbb{C}\\}\">\\(\\mathbb{F}\\in\\{\\mathbb{R},\\mathbb{C}\\}\\)</span> (scalar field)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_X:X\\times X\\to X\">\\(+_X:X\\times X\\to X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\odot:\\mathbb F\\times X\\to X\">\\(\\odot:\\mathbb F\\times X\\to X\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|\\cdot\\|\\in\\mathbb{R}_{\\geq0}^{X}\">\\(\\|\\cdot\\|\\in\\mathbb{R}_{\\geq0}^{X}\\)</span> (norm candidate)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span> (metric induced by the norm)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Norm}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Norm}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S\\)</span> (predicates defined here, with distinct fixed arities)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\)</span> (function and metric-space predicates)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> (vector-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}explicit}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{\\mathbb F}(X,+_X,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\n\\exists0_X\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\\forall x\\in X\\;(0_X+_Xx=x)\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb F\\;\\Bigl[(\\|x\\|=0\\leftrightarrow x=0_X)\\land\n\\|\\alpha\\odot x\\|=|\\alpha|\\,\\|x\\|\\land\\|x+_Xy\\|\\leq\\|x\\|+\\|y\\|\\bigr]\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}explicit}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{\\mathbb F}(X,+_X,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\n\\exists0_X\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\\forall x\\in X\\;(0_X+_Xx=x)\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb F\\;\\Bigl[(\\|x\\|=0\\leftrightarrow x=0_X)\\land\n\\|\\alpha\\odot x\\|=|\\alpha|\\,\\|x\\|\\land\\|x+_Xy\\|\\leq\\|x\\|+\\|y\\|\\bigr]\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}alias}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}alias}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}metric}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S(d,\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;d(x,y)=\\|x+_X((-1_{\\mathbb F})\\odot y)\\|\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}norm\\text{-}metric}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormMetric}_S(d,\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Norm}_S(\\|\\cdot\\|,X,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;d(x,y)=\\|x+_X((-1_{\\mathbb F})\\odot y)\\|\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The two-place existential projection is named <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedCarrier}_S\\)</span> so that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Norm}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Norm}_S\\)</span> retains its unique five-place signature.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span>-norm: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|f\\|_p = (\\int |f|^p)^{1/p}\">\\(\\|f\\|_p = (\\int |f|^p)^{1/p}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Operator norm: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|A\\| = \\sup_{\\|x\\| \\leq 1} \\|Ax\\|\">\\(\\|A\\| = \\sup_{\\|x\\| \\leq 1} \\|Ax\\|\\)</span></li>\n<li>Banach space: normed space complete in induced metric</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Conway, A Course in Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-vector-space","status":"resolved","id":"592f9cfb66a507c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depe